HST Office: the HASON TECH banner is shown in every user interface of every document window and in HST PDF.

Owner decision 14/11/2026: the banner can no longer be hidden by choosing another user interface, hiding or
customizing toolbars, or locking them. It always shows its artwork (never a text card), at least 260 x 75
logical px (the artwork's 360:104 ratio), in a strip at least that high.

- vcl: the banner moves from sfx2 to vcl so that framework and xmlsecurity can host it too. One engine,
  hst::banner::Core (vcl/source/control/HstBannerCore.*: content from org.hst.office.BannerFeed on worker
  threads, rotation, the one-second display count, click, painting), and two views (include/vcl/HstBanner.hxx):
  HstRibbonBanner, a VCL control, and HstBannerWidget, a weld drawing area. The compact artwork, unused since
  13/11, is gone. Worker results reach the main loop through user events that keep the core alive, so they
  never touch a view that went away. HstBannerGeometry.hxx moves to include/vcl, with the strip size helpers.
- Tabbed ribbon (notebookbar.ui of Writer, Calc, Impress and Draw): unchanged, beside the groups.
- Other notebookbars (tabbed compact, grouped compact, single and contextual single): NotebookBar tells
  whether its content shows a banner itself (NotebookbarTabControl claims it); otherwise the window border
  shows one at the right end of the bar's strip, which is at least 79 logical px high, with the bar to the
  left of it, centred vertically.
- Toolbar user interfaces (Standard, Single, Sidebar): framework's ToolbarLayoutManager keeps the banner at
  the right end of the top docking area of the windows of text documents, spreadsheets, presentations and
  drawings without a visible notebookbar. The top docking area is at least as high as the banner needs, also
  without any toolbar, and its rows take the width left of the banner, centred vertically beside it. Hiding,
  customizing or locking toolbars does not reach it; full screen hides it with the toolbars.
- HST PDF: the toolbar is two even rows of controls on the left and the banner at the right of the strip.
  HSTPdfInfo reports BannerScreen.

